      \field{abstract}{We present VisMorph, a live programming environment for shape-adaptive computers---systems composed of microscopic units that wirelessly coordinate to change shape and function. VisMorph supports intuitive application development for such systems through real-time visualization, interactive feedback, and a declarative programming language called MorphLang. It allows users to define physical layouts, specify behaviors, and visualize communication on a 2D grid, making development more intuitive and efficient. VisMorph streamlines the process of programming dynamic, reconfigurable interfaces, enabling advanced workflows for shape-changing systems.}
