      \field{abstract}{Welcome to the 17th ACM SIGPLAN International Workshop on Virtual Machines and Intermediate Languages (VMIL 2025). VMIL aims to advance the state of the art in the design and implementation of programming systems, with a particular focus on virtual machines---broadly defined. Co-located with ICFP/SPLASH\textquoteright{}25, the workshop took place in Singapore on October 15, 2025. The workshop featured two submission deadlines: the first for mature research and work-in-progress papers included in the proceedings, and the second for position papers, experience reports, new ideas, and emerging results. VMIL received twelve submissions this year: eight full-length research papers, one work-in-progress paper, and three position papers. An accomplished Program Committee evaluated submissions based on novelty, relevance, and contribution to the state of the art. Each research and work-in-progress paper received at least three reviews. In total, eight papers were accepted---four research papers, three work-in-progress papers, and one position paper for presentation. Accepted research and work-in-progress papers are also published in the ACM Digital Library. Submissions spanned a wide range of topics, including ahead-of-time and just-in-time compilation, interpreters, intermediate representations, developer tooling, and memory management. Anil Madhavapeddy delivered the keynote on post-POSIX IO interfaces. We thank the authors for their submissions, the Program Committee for their high-quality reviews, and all attendees for their participation. Yusuke Izawa, Shoaib Akram September 2025 VMIL Program Co-Chairs}
